{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/805994-rest-in-peace-david-bowie","id":805994,"title":"Rest in peace, David Bowie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T05:21:25-08:00","id":805994,"title":"Rest in peace, David Bowie","content":"I never got into David Bowie. My ears are deficient, and his singing voice just had some quality that played to my deficiency, making it difficult for me to comprehend what he was singing. Likewise, I never saw his movies; the ones he was in came out during times in my life when they weren't for me.<br /> <br /> Yet despite all this, the cult of personality surrounding Mr. Bowie is such that I felt intimately aware of him. Just through cultural osmosis, I felt familiar with him, or at least with the legend of him: charming; slyly bright; sexy in a way even a straight man has to give props to; warm.<br /> <br /> I have never met him, never corresponded with him, never seen his films, and can only name two of his songs; but despite all that, he has felt like a part of my life, and his loss saddens me.<br /> <br /> How much more, then, must his fans, his friends, and his family be feeling that loss?<br /> <br /> Mr. Bowie, thank you for everything you have been to the centuries you lived in, and I hope your rest is easy and peaceful, full of the knowledge that those who loved you in life love you still and will eventually find healing in that love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 01-11-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:20:43-08:00","id":806202,"title":"","content":"David Bowie was a cultural cornerstone to me all my life. I started with Labyrinth, and then found his music, and then found out about him as a person, and more beyond.<br /> <br /> As I said in the other thread, he has gone on to claim his rightful throne over mankind.<br /> <br /> Which is my way of saying I will miss him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:41:41-08:00","id":806225,"title":"","content":"I'm tempted to make some kind of joke about his music or something as a funny acknowledgement of his accomplishments, but that just wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> Rest in peace, Bowie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:50:39-08:00","id":806567,"title":"","content":"Google's main page doodle is about someone important to the suffragette movement on the day the man responsible for Suffragette City died.<br /> <br /> The universe loves a good synchronicity gag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:58:11-08:00","id":806573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/805994-rest-in-peace-david-bowie?p=806567#post806567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Google's main page doodle is about someone important to the suffragette movement on the day the man responsible for Suffragette City died.<br /> <br /> The universe loves a good synchronicity gag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently. <br /> <br /> Also, no worries, Promie. I made a tasteless blue joke about masturbating to Labyrinth on Twitter earlier. Proving simultaneously that I don't deal with loss well and that I'm a heartless, unfunny monster without redeeming factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:06:35-08:00","id":806582,"title":"","content":"A lot of Bowie was playing on the overhead at the grocery store today. Weird place to hear a tribute to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:45:26-08:00","id":806724,"title":"","content":"Rest in Peace Good Sir Bowie, I bought a bunch of his albums on Itunes today and listened to it throughout the day. A celebrity death hasn't hit me this hard in a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}